@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title SD Host Controller Simplified Specification Version 3.00

rectangle "Slot Interrupt Status Register (Offset 0FCh)" {
  |= D15 |= D08 | D07 |= D00 |
  | Rsvd | | Interrupt Signal For Each Slot | |
}

|= Location |= Attrib |= Register Field Explanation |
| 15-08 | Rsvd | **Reserved** |
| 07-00 | ROC | **Interrupt Signal For Each Slot** \nThese status bits indicate the logical OR of Interrupt Signal and Wakeup \nSignal for each slot. A maximum of 8 slots can be defined. If one interrupt \nsignal is associated with multiple slots, the Host Driver can know which \ninterrupt is generated by reading these status bits. By a power on reset or by \nsetting **Software Reset For All**, the interrupt signal shall be de-asserted \nand this status shall be read 00h. |

**Bit-to-Slot Mapping:**
|= Bit |= Slot |
| Bit 00 | Slot 1 |
| Bit 01 | Slot 2 |
| Bit 02 | Slot 3 |
| ....... | ....... |
| Bit 07 | Slot 8 |

newpage

rectangle "Host Controller Version Register (Offset 0FEh)" {
  |= D15 |= D08 | D07 |= D00 |
  | Vendor Version Number | | Specification Version Number | |
}

|= Location |= Attrib |= Register Field Explanation |
| 15-08 | HwInit | **Vendor Version Number** \nThis status is reserved for the vendor version number. The Host Driver \nshould not use this status. |
| 07-00 | HwInit | **Specification Version Number** \nThis status indicates the Host Controller Spec. Version. The upper and \nlower 4-bits indicate the version. |

**Specification Version Codes:**
|= Code |= Specification Version |
| 00h | SD Host Specification Version 1.00 |
| 01h | SD Host Specification Version 2.00 \nIncluding the feature of the ADMA and Test Register, |
| 02h | SD Host Specification Version 3.00 |
| others | Reserved |

@enduml